Rotting oranges — distances (minutes) from the rotten orange in the corner:

```text
grid         minute each orange rots
2 1 1        0 1 2
1 1 0        1 2 .
0 1 1        . 3 4
```

The largest minute is 4. If any fresh orange is never reached, the answer is −1 — so count fresh oranges at the start and decrease the count as they rot.

```cpp
queue<array<int, 3>> q;          // row, column, minute
// push every rotten orange with minute 0, count the fresh ones
while (!q.empty()) {
    auto [r, c, t] = q.front(); q.pop();
    minutes = max(minutes, t);
    for (int d = 0; d < 4; d++) {
        int nr = r + dr[d], nc = c + dc[d];
        if (nr >= 0 && nr < R && nc >= 0 && nc < C && g[nr][nc] == 1) {
            g[nr][nc] = 2; fresh--; q.push({nr, nc, t + 1});
        }
    }
}
```

